          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new word: what did samyak mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: शान्तिः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "शान्तिः (śāntiḥ) — \"peace, stillness\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "शान्तिः (śāntiḥ) is peace of a particular kind: not the absence of war so much as the settling of something that had been disturbed. It comes from śam, \"to grow calm, to come to rest\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A great many Sanskrit texts close on it, said three times over, once for each of the troubles a person can meet. You already have स्वस्ति for a wish of wellbeing; शान्तिः (śāntiḥ) is the quieter one, and the one you would say last."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A word for peace, and the way Sanskrit texts stop."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
