        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: सादरम्",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सादरम् (sādaram) — \"respectfully, with respect\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सादरम् (sādaram) is sa-, \"with\", joined to ādara, \"regard, esteem\" — so, \"with regard\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It goes at the front of a request, where English would put its politeness at the end of a letter. Set beside कृपया it makes a request about as courteous as Sanskrit gets: sādaram kṛpayā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A politeness that goes at the front rather than the end."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
