        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: प्रसन्नः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "प्रसन्नः (prasannaḥ) — \"pleased, gracious, clear\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "प्रसन्नः (prasannaḥ) describes a face that has cleared. The one word covers still water, a settled mind and a kindly host, because it is pra-, \"forth\", with sad, \"to settle\": what was cloudy has dropped its silt."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "To say that a guest left you प्रसन्नः (prasannaḥ) is to say they left you at ease. The offering handed back from a temple, prasāda, is this same word — grace, given a physical form."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A word for water, a mind and a host, all at once."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
