            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the last word of the chapter: what did abhinandanam mean, and what did śāntiḥ mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: आशीर्वादः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आशीर्वादः (āśīrvādaḥ) — \"a blessing\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आशीर्वादः (āśīrvādaḥ) is a blessing spoken aloud: āśis, \"a wish, a prayer\", joined to vāda, \"a speaking\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That second piece is the one inside धन्यवादः, the thanks you learned on your very first page — thanks is a speaking too. An elder gives आशीर्वादः (āśīrvādaḥ); you answer with धन्यवादः; and the two are built the same way, out of a wish and a word for saying it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five courtesies, and the piece shared by a blessing and a thanks."
            }
          ]
        },
